From 547a723795207913ee9876f6e49a08996f1e85c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:30:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/53] Next Command through the host app's AI provider in
 embedded builds

Embedded (remote_tty) builds have no Warp AI, so Next Command now asks the
host app (window.warpPanelNextCommand) with Warp's own request JSON, and the
host answers with its fast model. It's opt-in (host.ai.next_command, off by
default) and only runs while private routing is on, since it sends recent
commands and the last command's output. The planned "Next Command" settings
row becomes a real toggle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
